        "diagram": null
      },
      {
        "number": 3,
        "page": 2,
        "marks": 3,
        "stem": "During a practice session of long jump, a coach trains an athlete to take off the jump at an angle of 45°.\nDerive a mathematical expression for the maximum range of the athlete.",
        "choices": {},
        "facsimile": "/paper-crops/PHY-XI-2024-P2/q3.png",
        "diagram": null
      },
      {
        "number": 4,
        "page": 3,
        "marks": 2,
        "stem": "A solid disc with a moment of inertia of 0.125 kg·m² is rotating about its central axis with an angular velocity of 10 rad/s.\nCalculate the rotational kinetic energy of the disc.",
        "choices": {},
        "facsimile": "/paper-crops/PHY-XI-2024-P2/q4.png",
        "diagram": null
      },
      {
        "number": 5,
        "page": 3,
        "marks": 3,
        "stem": "State any THREE conditions for the generation of turbulent flow.",
        "choices": {},
        "facsimile": "/paper-crops/PHY-XI-2024-P2/q5.png",
        "diagram": null
      },
      {
        "number": 6,
        "page": 3,
        "marks": 2,
        "stem": "Rameen observes a simple pendulum oscillating between P and Q, over the mean position O as shown in the diagram.\nShe claims that in one complete vibration, the distance covered by the bob is $2x$ units.\nDo you agree with Rameen’s claim? Justify your stance with a reason.",
        "choices": {},
        "facsimile": "/paper-crops/PHY-XI-2024-P2/q6.png",
