      },
      {
        "number": 7,
        "page": 4,
        "marks": 3,
        "stem": "Explain how stationary waves are produced in an air column organ pipes.",
        "choices": {},
        "facsimile": "/paper-crops/PHY-XI-2024-P2/q7.png",
        "diagram": null
      },
      {
        "number": 8,
        "page": 4,
        "marks": 3,
        "stem": "The wavelength of light in air is $4.0\\times10^{-4}\\,\\mathrm m$. It is incident perpendicularly on a double slit and passes through the slits. The slit separation is $2.0\\times10^{-2}\\,\\mathrm m$, and bright and dark fringes are observed on a screen 2 m away from the slits.\nCalculate the distance between the two adjacent bright fringes on the screen.",
        "choices": {},
        "facsimile": "/paper-crops/PHY-XI-2024-P2/q8.png",
        "diagram": null
      },
      {
        "number": 9,
        "page": 5,
        "marks": 7,
        "stem": "EITHER\na.\nDerive an expression for the energy required to escape a body from the Earth’s gravitational field.\nOR\nb.\nWhen a net force acts on an object, the work done on the object equals the change in its kinetic\nenergy.\nBased on the given principle, derive work-energy equation in the presence of friction.",
        "choices": {},
        "facsimile": "/paper-crops/PHY-XI-2024-P2/q9.png",
